<p>Most property claims are first estimated before anyone has opened a wall, pulled up flooring or torn off a roof. That is why <strong>insurance claim supplements in Port Arthur</strong> are such a normal part of the process. Once repairs begin, contractors find rotted decking, a second layer of shingles, wet insulation or framing damage that no one could see during the first inspection. Prices change, code requirements surface and items that were simply missed come to light. A supplement asks the insurer to add those items to the claim, with documentation that shows why they belong.</p>

<h2>When a Supplement Is Appropriate</h2>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Trigger</th><th>Example</th><th>What supports it</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Hidden damage found during repairs</td><td>Water-damaged roof decking discovered at tear-off</td><td>Photos before covering, measurements, contractor notes</td></tr>
